WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:01.230
- You play a therapist

00:00:01.230 --> 00:00:02.130
- I do.
- on Shrinking, a very

00:00:02.130 --> 00:00:02.963
funny one.

00:00:02.963 --> 00:00:03.900
- Thank you.
- So, tell us about the show.

00:00:03.900 --> 00:00:05.610
- Thank you, Yeah, so I
play this character named

00:00:05.610 --> 00:00:07.710
Gabby, on Shrinking, which is on Apple TV,

00:00:07.710 --> 00:00:10.830
and she works with Jimmy,
played by Jason Segel

00:00:10.830 --> 00:00:13.710
and Paul, who's our boss,
played by Harrison Ford.

00:00:13.710 --> 00:00:17.970
And Jimmy, Jimmy's character is grieving

00:00:17.970 --> 00:00:19.860
because his wife suddenly passed away.

00:00:19.860 --> 00:00:21.990
And I, they brought me onto the show,

00:00:21.990 --> 00:00:23.190
it's done by Bill Lawrence,

00:00:23.190 --> 00:00:25.680
and Brett Goldstein of
like The Lasso crew,

00:00:25.680 --> 00:00:27.420
and they brought me on the show 'cause

00:00:27.420 --> 00:00:29.310
they wanted my character to really balance

00:00:29.310 --> 00:00:31.500
out like, Harrison Ford's surliness,

00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:33.780
and then Jason's just
doing the Jason thing.

00:00:33.780 --> 00:00:34.613
- (laughing)

00:00:34.613 --> 00:00:36.180
- So they really wanted they wanted her to

00:00:36.180 --> 00:00:37.650
come in and balance everything out.

00:00:37.650 --> 00:00:39.300
And you can see in that office

00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:41.640
from that clip that she's
very bright and colorful

00:00:41.640 --> 00:00:43.701
and bubbly and it's really
fun because I get to be

00:00:43.701 --> 00:00:44.534
- [Kelly] Very funny.

00:00:44.534 --> 00:00:47.820
- Yeah, it's fun to be like
this, like bubbly, you know,

00:00:47.820 --> 00:00:51.000
millennial black lady,
like saying "panties"

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:52.190
to Harrison Ford.

00:00:52.190 --> 00:00:53.490
- (laughing and clapping)

00:00:53.490 --> 00:00:54.573
- Like that rules.

00:00:54.573 --> 00:00:55.512
- I'm sure he's Heard
that before. (laughs)

00:00:55.512 --> 00:00:56.345
(crowd laughs)

00:00:56.345 --> 00:00:59.371
- And it is, I think he's
heard it as "panties",

00:00:59.371 --> 00:01:00.990
but then there's like
the black part of it,

00:01:00.990 --> 00:01:02.580
which is like, oh, growing up,

00:01:02.580 --> 00:01:03.810
like I didn't know until I was older

00:01:03.810 --> 00:01:06.240
that it's not pan-teez,
it's paneez like, it's like,

00:01:06.240 --> 00:01:08.422
- Oh, I don't know, I'm
Southern, we say paneez.

00:01:08.422 --> 00:01:09.573
- [Jessica] It's paneez, right?

00:01:09.573 --> 00:01:10.590
Yeah, But a lot of women go "pahnteez".

00:01:10.590 --> 00:01:11.844
- Oh.

00:01:11.844 --> 00:01:12.677
(crowd laughing)

00:01:12.677 --> 00:01:14.070
- Like "pahnteez", it's my "pahnteez".

00:01:14.070 --> 00:01:14.904
Right, Seth?

00:01:14.904 --> 00:01:16.032
- I call 'em my "pahnteez".

00:01:16.032 --> 00:01:17.490
(all laughing)

00:01:17.490 --> 00:01:19.170
- I just love that people say "pahnteez".

00:01:19.170 --> 00:01:20.850
- [Jessica] It's "pahnteez".

00:01:20.850 --> 00:01:22.500
